; knowsia.com — Cloudflare import draft.
; Compiled 2026-09-04 from live DNS lookups; TXT records added 2026-09-12 from
; CyberPanel → DNS → knowsia.com (they could not be read remotely — see below).
; Doc 20 (Domain Consolidation) Phase 0. Import via Cloudflare → DNS → Import and Export.
;
; WHY THE TXT RECORDS HAD TO BE READ BY HAND: every nameserver delegated for
; knowsia.com is unreachable. ns1/ns2.knowsia.com have no A record at all, and
; ns1/ns2/ns3.noohrabusiness.com all resolve to 127.0.0.1. The domain currently
; resolves ONLY from stale resolver caches (A, MX and SOA were cached; TXT was
; not, which is why TXT queries time out and TCP connections are closed). When
; those caches expire, knowsia.com stops resolving entirely — website, mail,
; reg.knowsia.com and the 312 printed /verify/KNS-… URLs with it.
; Moving to Cloudflare is therefore a REPAIR, not just migration preparation.
;
; ── THREE FAULTS FOUND IN THE LIVE ZONE, FIXED HERE (2026-09-12) ────────────
;
; 1. TWO SPF RECORDS AT THE APEX. CyberPanel's zone lists
;    "v=spf1 a mx ip4:64.20.36.232 ~all" on knowsia.com TWICE. Under RFC 7208
;    §4.5 a domain publishing more than one SPF record is a PERMERROR, and
;    receivers must treat it as such — so SPF is not merely invisible, it is
;    FAILING, and has been for as long as the duplicate has existed. Exactly one
;    SPF record appears below. Delete the duplicate in CyberPanel too, or it
;    comes back if that zone is ever re-exported.
;
; 2. DUPLICATE DKIM SELECTOR. default._domainkey.knowsia.com is also listed
;    twice. Two TXT records at one selector make the key ambiguous and
;    verification unreliable. One below.
;
; 3. DKIM IS IN TEST MODE. _domainkey.knowsia.com carries "t=y; o=~;" — t=y
;    tells receivers this domain is only TESTING DKIM and not to act on
;    failures, which throws away most of the benefit. It is dropped here. (o=~
;    is ADSP, withdrawn as a standard in 2013, and is dropped with it.)
;
; A fourth, not a mail problem but broken: the live zone has
; "_acme-challenge.quiz.knowsia.com.knowsia.com" — the zone name appended to a
; name that was already fully qualified, a CyberPanel UI trap. It can never
; validate. Written correctly below.
;
; NOT a fault, recorded because it looked like one: the DKIM record is stored as
; THREE quoted strings, which is correct — a single DNS TXT string cannot exceed
; 255 bytes. The key was read out in full on 2026-09-12 and verified as a valid
; 2048-bit RSA public key. So the TXT-serving failure described above is NOT
; caused by a malformed DKIM record, and its real cause is unknown — which no
; longer matters, because Cloudflare becomes authoritative and serves these
; records correctly regardless.
;
; STILL NEEDED: the Google Search Console token. Do NOT try to recover the
; truncated one — a fresh Domain property issues a new value (Doc 20 Phase 0
; step 1), and that is the one to publish.
;
; TTLs are deliberately short (300 s) for the migration window. Raise to 3600 once stable.
;
; Cloudflare proxy status: import with DNS-only (grey cloud) for EVERY record. Vercel and
; the mail host need direct connections; the orange-cloud proxy in front of Vercel breaks TLS
; and caching assumptions.

$ORIGIN knowsia.com.
$TTL 300

; ---------- Apex and www (TODAY: WordPress on the VPS) ----------
; Phase 3 changes these two lines to:  @ A 76.76.21.21   and   www CNAME cname.vercel-dns.com.
@                 300  IN  A      64.20.36.232
www               300  IN  CNAME  knowsia.com.

; ---------- Mail (on the VPS — CyberPanel / Roundcube). Must move before Phase 4 ----------
@                 300  IN  MX 10  knowsia.com.
mail              300  IN  A      64.20.36.232

; SPF — EXACTLY ONE. See fault 1 above.
@                 300  IN  TXT    "v=spf1 a mx ip4:64.20.36.232 ~all"

; DKIM — one selector, test mode removed. Key read from CyberPanel 2026-09-12
; and VERIFIED: 392 base64 chars → 294 bytes DER → a valid 2048-bit RSA public
; key (checked with `cryptography`, not eyeballed — a truncated DKIM key FAILS
; verification rather than being ignored, so "it looks long enough" is not a
; check).
;
; Split into three strings because a single DNS TXT string cannot exceed 255
; bytes. The joins are load-bearing: a space BEFORE "p=" and NO space inside
; the base64. Whitespace in the middle of the key breaks it silently.
default._domainkey 300 IN  TXT    ( "v=DKIM1; h=sha256; k=rsa; "
                                    "p=MIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEAqABgfCbHRMCCNttqTM7s+eCaKpP7t0/a1HdAb+0uRg3mcgVFN4bUHh+XVo4naNaJMAE4zUUmZErk9/AD4Ssb/nfQBqCjG3YJjbtJuc5SGfai9x/4rgiQ0wws0NPoGXdCnaGsDlZ1CK7DuTk8DFA6HubmBmS7qbu1n/aFSEHlUl7tZ/fBiC1fU+kSG9ZsieaRPBFR4pJmsbBzAG"
                                    "diLk29VJMILF90hrh58RD3biUGLvSvrx7qkqkzWO3KuajKZWQlPfSXJUvrVzo/9KarqyT0WzyU06tLQOa+6BmypI0oIOG3lShSasNz0E7aAVoH3eWLFsyo6ZKTk1dfvtEQ+mOqlwIDAQAB" )

; DMARC. p=none is monitoring only: it reports nothing and enforces nothing.
; `rua` is added so the reports actually arrive somewhere — without it, p=none
; is a record that does literally nothing. Move to p=quarantine once the
; reports show legitimate mail passing (weeks, not days).
_dmarc            300  IN  TXT    "v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:info@knowsia.com"

; ---------- Transactional mail (Resend, via Amazon SES) ----------
; Already configured in the live zone, which means Resend's DNS side is DONE —
; only RESEND_API_KEY is missing on Railway (see PLAN.md: the whole trial
; conversion sequence is silently not sending).
send              300  IN  TXT    "v=spf1 include:amazonses.com ~all"
resend._domainkey 300  IN  TXT    "p=MIGfMA0GCSqGSIb3DQEBAQUAA4GNADCBiQKBgQC4Cmhh2…REPLACE-WITH-FULL-KEY"

; ---------- Applications ----------
reg               300  IN  CNAME  da623ee62209f472.vercel-dns-017.com.
; quiz.knowsia.com is BROKEN as of 2026-09-04: https://quiz.knowsia.com/ answers
; 301 to itself (a redirect loop) while https://knowsia-quiz-app.web.app/ is
; fine. A bare CNAME to the web.app host is not how Firebase Hosting custom
; domains work — the domain has to be added in the Firebase console
; (Hosting → Add custom domain), which issues a TXT verification record and
; two A records (Firebase's anycast IPs) to use INSTEAD of this CNAME. Keep the
; line below only until that is done, then replace it with what the console gives.
quiz              300  IN  CNAME  knowsia-quiz-app.web.app.
quiz              300  IN  TXT    "hosting-site=knowsia-quiz-app"
; Fault 4: the live zone has this name with ".knowsia.com" appended twice.
_acme-challenge.quiz 300 IN TXT   "NY3wQmMdbp3YUTNWZKhQh7fdeqzYHPSX-tdABbaZ160"
; Phase 1 adds:
; app               300  IN  CNAME  cname.vercel-dns.com.
; Phase 3 adds (VPS kept reachable for 60–90 days, noindex):
; legacy            300  IN  A      64.20.36.232

; ---------- Legacy hosting conveniences (VPS) ----------
ftp               300  IN  CNAME  knowsia.com.

; ---------- Nameserver glue (drop once Cloudflare is authoritative) ----------
; These are listed as authoritative for the domain and DO NOT RESOLVE today,
; which is the outage described in the header. Keep for 7 days after the
; registrar switch in case anything cached still asks, then delete.
ns1               300  IN  A      64.20.36.232
ns2               300  IN  A      64.20.36.232

; ---------- Verification records ----------
; Google Search Console. The value in CyberPanel's table view is cut off at
; "…04H96-"; a Search Console token is 43 characters after the "=", so CONFIRM
; the full string before importing — a truncated token silently fails to verify.
@                 300  IN  TXT    "google-site-verification=UaJeCu6p0HnWs8PU04H96-REPLACE-WITH-FULL-TOKEN"
; Vercel domain verification for knowsia.com (Vercel → course-registration → Domains shows the
; exact TXT name/value when you add the domain):
; _vercel           300  IN  TXT    "vc-domain-verify=knowsia.com,..."

; ---------- Deliberately NOT carried over ----------
; The live zone also holds SPF / DMARC / _domainkey records for the
; mail.knowsia.com SUBDOMAIN. Nothing sends as @mail.knowsia.com, and a
; subdomain SPF only matters if mail claims to come from it. Left out to keep
; the zone honest; add back if a mail client is ever configured to use it.
; Also left out: "_domainkey.knowsia.com  t=y; o=~;" — see fault 3.
